4. Electronegativity and Ionization Measures: Sanderson electronegativity and ionization potential (e.g., Me, Mi, SdssC, SdO).
5. Topological Connectivity/Structure: Topological indices (e.g., LOC, TI2_L, nCIR, SpPosA_B(p)).
6. Functional Group Features: Frequency or presence of specific functional groups (e.g., nArCOOR, nArNO2, NssssC, B01[C-Br], B03[C-Cl], B04[C-Br]).

These descriptor groups provide key dimensions to understand biodegradability based on atomic makeup, molecular structure, electronic properties, and functional group reactivity.

